WEBVTT

00:00:10.520 --> 00:00:13.260
Baira…  Genome…

00:00:13.940 --> 00:00:18.260
I promise to capture the Ignis!

00:00:20.740 --> 00:00:23.600
No one can capture me anymore.

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:26.820
It’s perfect.

00:00:26.820 --> 00:00:29.400
You’ve done well too.  Nice job.

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:30.980
Thank you.

00:00:31.570 --> 00:00:34.890
Yusaku will be surprised.

00:00:40.490 --> 00:00:42.990
Don’t laugh harder than me!

00:00:57.620 --> 00:01:00.750
I run Across the universe

00:01:00.890 --> 00:01:03.920
At the speed of light

00:01:04.320 --> 00:01:05.790
Begin Loading

00:01:06.030 --> 00:01:09.530
Open the door of dreams

00:01:10.030 --> 00:01:13.100
VRAINS spreads

00:01:13.330 --> 00:01:16.200
Believe in myself

00:01:16.440 --> 00:01:19.740
VRAINS continues

00:01:19.970 --> 00:01:25.050
The circuit draws the future

00:01:25.310 --> 00:01:29.120
I'll grab it with my own hands  Yeah

00:01:29.480 --> 00:01:30.720
Access!

00:01:30.780 --> 00:01:33.420
Start swirling, Data Storm!

00:01:33.690 --> 00:01:35.020
I'm now With the Wind

00:01:35.190 --> 00:01:37.320
Link with my soul

00:01:37.420 --> 00:01:40.090
Speed up, Data Storm!

00:01:40.290 --> 00:01:41.830
Now Win the Race

00:01:41.930 --> 00:01:44.670
Connected world

00:01:44.930 --> 00:01:48.170
No matter when

00:01:48.400 --> 00:01:51.540
Nothing is impossible

00:01:51.740 --> 00:01:55.680
Strive for hope

00:01:55.860 --> 00:02:00.250
And ride the wind!

00:02:18.760 --> 00:02:23.820
Thanks to the removal program, 
Another talk has died down.

00:02:23.820 --> 00:02:29.300
Since the virus's creator released 
the antidote, it was very effective.

00:02:32.180 --> 00:02:33.370
What’s wrong?

00:02:33.370 --> 00:02:37.510
We've been battling the Knights 
of Hanoi only inside LINK VRAINS.

00:02:37.510 --> 00:02:43.840
But this time, I realized that 
we were battling real people.

00:02:44.790 --> 00:02:48.980
Yeah.  There's still one 
Another mastermind left.

00:02:57.290 --> 00:03:00.560
He’s not Playmaker either.

00:03:00.560 --> 00:03:04.730
We can't remain spectators!

00:03:04.730 --> 00:03:09.000
Playmaker and Blue Angel are 
fighting the Knights of Hanoi!

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:09.800
So?

00:03:09.800 --> 00:03:14.320
The Duel Club is on break.  
But as duelists, we should-

00:03:14.320 --> 00:03:15.580
Don't do it.

00:03:15.580 --> 00:03:17.100
Why not?

00:03:17.100 --> 00:03:18.520
Three reasons.

00:03:18.520 --> 00:03:23.750
#1: There’s now a website for the removal 
program, so there are fewer Anothers.

00:03:23.750 --> 00:03:27.480
#2: You have no plan, so you’ll get burned.

00:03:27.480 --> 00:03:30.860
#3: Deep down inside, you’re scared.

00:03:30.860 --> 00:03:33.560
What?  I’m scared?

00:03:34.070 --> 00:03:37.410
That’s why you're going 
to ask me to join you.

00:03:39.310 --> 00:03:42.470
I picked the wrong person 
to discuss this with!

00:03:42.740 --> 00:03:45.480
Oh my.  You went too far, Yusaku.

00:03:45.480 --> 00:03:46.710
Be quiet.

00:04:01.320 --> 00:04:03.370
I’m Naoki Shima!

00:04:03.370 --> 00:04:06.990
I put my pride on the line during duels!

00:04:08.200 --> 00:04:11.200
In my duels, I'm full speed ahead!

00:04:11.200 --> 00:04:12.740
I won’t back down!

00:04:12.740 --> 00:04:14.980
I always move forward!

00:04:16.010 --> 00:04:18.370
My goal is to become the top duelist!

00:04:20.600 --> 00:04:23.880
Actually, within the top 50.

00:04:25.100 --> 00:04:27.340
Then you're not reaching for the top.

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:33.740
I appreciate your passion and 
enthusiasm.  But just those.

00:04:33.740 --> 00:04:35.800
Welcome to the Duel Club!

00:04:35.800 --> 00:04:38.760
-Welcome!  Let's study hard!
-Okay!

00:04:40.430 --> 00:04:43.480
Just my passion and enthusiasm…

00:04:44.360 --> 00:04:47.100
All show and no substance.

00:04:47.100 --> 00:04:49.240
When the going gets tough...

00:04:52.080 --> 00:04:54.210
Downloading new data.

00:04:55.390 --> 00:04:57.030
What’s going on?

00:04:57.030 --> 00:04:59.140
I didn't download this!

00:05:00.240 --> 00:05:02.610
Cyberse Wizard?

00:05:02.610 --> 00:05:05.610
I summon Cyberse Wizard!

00:05:08.770 --> 00:05:12.260
It’s Playmaker’s…  Why?

00:05:13.630 --> 00:05:17.600
"Be one with the Cyberse.  -PM"

00:05:17.600 --> 00:05:21.860
PM…  You mean Playmaker?

00:05:21.860 --> 00:05:23.600
This means…

00:05:26.050 --> 00:05:28.700
Shima, be one with the Cyberse.

00:05:28.700 --> 00:05:30.960
Be one with the Cyberse!

00:05:32.610 --> 00:05:37.080
Playmaker has chosen me?

00:05:38.960 --> 00:05:44.520
Aww, Playmaker!  You could've 
contacted me sooner!

00:05:44.520 --> 00:05:46.060
You’re so shy!

00:05:46.460 --> 00:05:49.890
Fujiki, I’m going first!

00:05:50.620 --> 00:05:55.580
Into the V-V-VRAINS!

00:06:01.060 --> 00:06:03.440
I'm in LINK VRAINS!

00:06:04.330 --> 00:06:06.450
This is virtual?

00:06:08.350 --> 00:06:10.930
It’s practically real!

00:06:12.660 --> 00:06:16.880
Wow!  I really feel like I’m walking!

00:06:16.880 --> 00:06:19.640
This is incredible!

00:06:20.860 --> 00:06:23.330
I’m gonna run!

00:06:24.730 --> 00:06:26.690
I can even feel the wind!

00:06:29.290 --> 00:06:31.090
Ouch!

00:06:33.540 --> 00:06:35.840
I can even feel pain!

00:06:35.840 --> 00:06:39.140
LINK VRAINS is incredi-

00:06:45.710 --> 00:06:47.650
Not him either.

00:06:52.250 --> 00:06:53.930
Save me!

00:06:54.820 --> 00:07:00.850
Am I in the middle of a Playmaker hunt?

00:07:00.850 --> 00:07:03.230
I’ve never seen you before.

00:07:06.900 --> 00:07:08.520
Just another weakling.

00:07:08.850 --> 00:07:10.980
W-Weakling?

00:07:11.470 --> 00:07:13.980
Shima, be one with the Cyberse.

00:07:16.360 --> 00:07:17.420
You’re wrong.

00:07:17.970 --> 00:07:21.390
I’m the only one deemed 
worthy by Playmaker!

00:07:21.390 --> 00:07:23.370
Such nonsense.

00:07:24.680 --> 00:07:27.300
Here's proof!

00:07:27.300 --> 00:07:29.770
A Cyberse card?

00:07:36.840 --> 00:07:40.130
I'm the duelist everyone 
will be talking about!

00:07:40.130 --> 00:07:43.460
The one who carries on Playmaker’s will!

00:07:43.460 --> 00:07:48.180
My name is Lonely Brave!

00:07:48.180 --> 00:07:52.370
I’ll defeat you quickly and force 
you to tell me where Playmaker is.

00:07:53.690 --> 00:07:56.430
Fine!  I’ll take you on!

00:07:56.920 --> 00:08:00.130
This is bad!  Seriously?

00:08:00.130 --> 00:08:03.660
My first battle is against a Knight of Hanoi?

00:08:04.860 --> 00:08:06.180
Duel!

00:08:10.770 --> 00:08:12.410
What's this?

00:08:12.780 --> 00:08:16.090
Three Level 5s and a Level 10.

00:08:16.090 --> 00:08:18.380
This hand is a disaster!

00:08:25.100 --> 00:08:28.540
Oh no!  Five Level 7s?

00:08:28.540 --> 00:08:31.260
This hand is a disaster!

00:08:37.060 --> 00:08:39.200
My hand is perfect!

00:08:39.200 --> 00:08:42.210
I have to do something about this…

00:08:43.770 --> 00:08:45.400
I go first!

00:08:46.210 --> 00:08:47.370
Fine.

00:08:47.370 --> 00:08:48.780
Thank goodness!

00:08:48.780 --> 00:08:53.090
From my hand, I activate the 
Quick-Play Spell, Hand Destruction!

00:08:54.240 --> 00:08:58.180
We both discard two cards from our hands.

00:08:58.180 --> 00:09:01.110
Then we both draw two cards from our decks!

00:09:01.790 --> 00:09:06.030
All right!  Good job, Knight of Hanoi!

00:09:06.360 --> 00:09:10.040
I send two Steelswarm 
Mantises to the graveyard!

00:09:10.970 --> 00:09:13.700
Now you select two!

00:09:13.700 --> 00:09:18.180
I choose two Green Baboons, 
Defenders of the Forest!

00:09:20.140 --> 00:09:21.610
This draw…

00:09:21.610 --> 00:09:23.580
...will determine everything!

00:09:29.080 --> 00:09:30.550
Mediocre.

00:09:31.540 --> 00:09:34.710
Wait a sec.  A Feather of the Phoenix...

00:09:34.990 --> 00:09:38.530
Yes.  This will work.

00:09:39.840 --> 00:09:41.500
It was a perfect draw!

00:09:43.320 --> 00:09:45.320
It was perfect for me too.

00:09:45.320 --> 00:09:48.940
Oh no!  It was perfect for him?

00:09:48.940 --> 00:09:54.210
Here I go!  I activate the spell 
card, A Feather of the Phoenix!

00:09:54.520 --> 00:10:01.690
I discard one card to select a card in my 
graveyard and return it to the top of my deck!

00:10:01.690 --> 00:10:04.420
I discard Steelswarm Mantis!

00:10:04.420 --> 00:10:06.890
I return Hand Destruction from my graveyard!

00:10:06.890 --> 00:10:10.870
From my hand, I activate the 
spell card, Soul Charge!

00:10:11.360 --> 00:10:14.820
I Special Summon as many monsters 
from my graveyard as I want!

00:10:14.820 --> 00:10:20.100
But for every monster I Special 
Summon, I lose 1000 LP.

00:10:20.280 --> 00:10:23.340
Come, three Steelswarm Mantises!

00:10:32.060 --> 00:10:34.790
The opponent has 1000 LP left.

00:10:36.140 --> 00:10:39.840
This is bad!  He summoned 
three high Level monsters!

00:10:40.240 --> 00:10:45.530
But I have 2600 ATK Baboons in my graveyard.

00:10:45.530 --> 00:10:48.660
If I resurrect them, I'll 
destroy his monsters!

00:10:49.040 --> 00:10:53.640
I know you’re planning 
to resurrect your Baboons.

00:10:53.850 --> 00:10:55.400
Gulp!

00:10:56.180 --> 00:10:58.110
Maybe, maybe not.

00:10:58.110 --> 00:11:00.110
He sees right through me!

00:11:00.110 --> 00:11:02.010
Too bad!

00:11:02.010 --> 00:11:06.980
I tribute three Steelswarms 
to Tribute Summon!

00:11:08.820 --> 00:11:11.560
Come, Steelswarm Hercules!

00:11:20.500 --> 00:11:23.900
Level 10.  3200 ATK.

00:11:24.720 --> 00:11:26.010
Not bad.

00:11:26.010 --> 00:11:28.440
I’m done for...

00:11:28.770 --> 00:11:35.340
Once per turn, by paying half my 
LP, it can destroy all other cards.

00:11:36.340 --> 00:11:43.280
So no matter what monsters you bring out, 
they'll all be destroyed on my next turn.

00:11:43.280 --> 00:11:45.920
I'm totally done for.

00:11:45.920 --> 00:11:47.590
I end my turn!

00:11:47.590 --> 00:11:50.570
Bring it on, Playmaker’s associate!

00:11:50.960 --> 00:11:52.920
My name is Lonely Brave!

00:11:52.920 --> 00:11:56.700
The only one deemed worthy by Playmaker!

00:11:58.080 --> 00:12:00.440
My turn!  I draw!

00:12:05.980 --> 00:12:07.080
It's here.

00:12:07.080 --> 00:12:09.540
Cyberse Wizard.

00:12:09.540 --> 00:12:15.550
It’s good that I got it, but 
how am I supposed to use it?

00:12:15.850 --> 00:12:17.750
I know you can use it.

00:12:18.560 --> 00:12:22.560
I’m always with you.

00:12:22.560 --> 00:12:26.530
Just like how you always watched me.

00:12:26.780 --> 00:12:29.500
Always watched…

00:12:32.280 --> 00:12:35.300
Oh yeah.  That’s right!

00:12:35.300 --> 00:12:37.470
I’ve always watched him.

00:12:38.220 --> 00:12:40.940
So I know how to use it!

00:12:41.420 --> 00:12:44.340
I can do it.  I can do it.  I can do it!

00:12:44.340 --> 00:12:47.650
What’s he muttering to himself?

00:12:47.650 --> 00:12:49.980
Here I go, Knight of Hanoi!

00:12:49.980 --> 00:12:53.120
I summon Cyberse Wizard!

00:13:02.330 --> 00:13:03.320
Yusaku!

00:13:03.320 --> 00:13:04.820
Good timing.

00:13:04.820 --> 00:13:06.070
Look at this.

00:13:07.020 --> 00:13:08.200
What's up?

00:13:09.300 --> 00:13:11.540
Cyberse Wizard?

00:13:12.130 --> 00:13:16.510
Someone other than you or 
Revolver has summoned a Cyberse.

00:13:18.900 --> 00:13:20.240
Lonely Brave.

00:13:20.240 --> 00:13:22.280
I’ve never seen him before.

00:13:22.280 --> 00:13:24.480
That’s a cool name.

00:13:24.480 --> 00:13:25.720
Is it?

00:13:25.720 --> 00:13:27.650
Well, not as cool as Ai.

00:13:27.650 --> 00:13:29.720
But I have the card.

00:13:32.140 --> 00:13:35.190
Oh my!  It's missing its data!

00:13:35.190 --> 00:13:36.660
The data?

00:13:36.660 --> 00:13:39.650
You have an empty card.

00:13:39.650 --> 00:13:41.210
What’s going on?

00:13:41.210 --> 00:13:43.690
Who knows.

00:13:53.530 --> 00:13:55.250
Cyberse?

00:13:55.840 --> 00:13:58.730
Cyberse Wizard’s effect activates!

00:13:58.730 --> 00:14:04.620
Once per turn, your monster changes 
from attack to defense position!

00:14:04.620 --> 00:14:07.660
Cyberse Algorithm!

00:14:10.530 --> 00:14:13.080
You have 1000 LP left.

00:14:13.080 --> 00:14:17.620
You overly hurt yourself to 
bring out a Level 10 monster!

00:14:17.850 --> 00:14:19.820
Here I go!  Battle!

00:14:19.820 --> 00:14:23.580
Cyberse Wizard attacks Steelswarm Hercules!

00:14:23.580 --> 00:14:29.400
Umm…  On the turn Cyberse 
Algorithm is activated…

00:14:29.400 --> 00:14:34.700
Umm…  Due to my Cyberse’s 
effect…  Umm…

00:14:34.700 --> 00:14:44.280
If it attacks a monster that was switched to 
defense position, it deals piercing damage.

00:14:45.370 --> 00:14:48.000
You take battle damage!

00:14:48.000 --> 00:14:50.740
Illusion Spike!

00:14:58.910 --> 00:15:04.760
You have no right to call yourself a duelist!

00:15:06.050 --> 00:15:10.780
That Cyberse Wizard was 
stolen from Yusaku’s deck?

00:15:10.780 --> 00:15:15.720
Maybe Lonely Brave is the 
mastermind behind the Anothers.

00:15:16.160 --> 00:15:19.640
Then why would he duel a Knight of Hanoi?

00:15:20.150 --> 00:15:23.200
In order to draw out Playmaker.

00:15:23.200 --> 00:15:24.110
Kusanagi.

00:15:24.400 --> 00:15:25.560
Leave it to me.

00:15:27.560 --> 00:15:29.230
He defeated a Knight of Hanoi.

00:15:29.230 --> 00:15:30.810
Using a Cyberse!

00:15:30.810 --> 00:15:32.460
Wow!

00:15:33.200 --> 00:15:36.650
I'm the one who carries 
on Playmaker’s will.

00:15:36.650 --> 00:15:41.460
Lonely Brave-  No, I’m not alone.

00:15:41.460 --> 00:15:43.760
My courage is everyone’s courage!

00:15:45.680 --> 00:15:48.230
I’m abandoning my Lonely name.

00:15:48.840 --> 00:15:51.870
Starting now, my name is Brave Max!

00:15:51.870 --> 00:15:54.200
Max!

00:15:54.200 --> 00:15:56.720
Max!

00:15:56.720 --> 00:15:58.170
Thank you!

00:15:59.890 --> 00:16:02.170
He'll lead me to Playmaker.

00:16:02.170 --> 00:16:04.650
And to the Ignis.

00:16:07.420 --> 00:16:09.080
Found you.

00:16:09.600 --> 00:16:12.790
Shima is Lonely Brave?

00:16:13.210 --> 00:16:16.250
Well, he just evolved into Brave Max.

00:16:16.490 --> 00:16:18.000
There’s no mistake.

00:16:18.000 --> 00:16:20.460
It's your classmate.

00:16:21.210 --> 00:16:24.800
If the mastermind learns 
that he used a Cyberse…

00:16:25.550 --> 00:16:27.440
Shima is in danger.

00:16:29.250 --> 00:16:32.770
I’m already LINK VRAINS’ newest legend!

00:16:32.770 --> 00:16:36.920
The hottest duelist!  I'm trending!

00:16:36.920 --> 00:16:39.150
Because I’m Playmaker’s-

00:16:39.150 --> 00:16:41.080
You’re Playmaker’s what?

00:16:54.890 --> 00:16:59.400
Sorry.  But in order to capture the Ignis…

00:17:02.370 --> 00:17:03.900
Where am I?

00:17:03.900 --> 00:17:06.190
What is this place?  Hey!

00:17:06.190 --> 00:17:07.770
Awake?

00:17:08.850 --> 00:17:12.320
Who are you?  What’s going on?

00:17:12.700 --> 00:17:14.360
I’ll tell you what I want.

00:17:14.720 --> 00:17:17.070
Call Playmaker.

00:17:17.460 --> 00:17:22.300
Playmaker?  I don’t know how to call him!

00:17:22.710 --> 00:17:27.670
Then I'll use you to lure Playmaker.

00:17:27.670 --> 00:17:28.770
Lure?

00:17:29.180 --> 00:17:31.340
What's going on?

00:17:31.340 --> 00:17:33.550
What’s going to happen to me?

00:17:36.700 --> 00:17:40.270
I'm being turned into Another?

00:17:40.270 --> 00:17:44.680
Stop it!  Stop!  Help me!

00:17:45.430 --> 00:17:47.150
Brave Max has appeared!

00:17:47.150 --> 00:17:49.390
Along with a Knight of Hanoi.

00:17:49.850 --> 00:17:51.410
Can you get closer?

00:17:51.410 --> 00:17:52.650
Hold on.

00:17:54.060 --> 00:17:56.860
Who are you?

00:17:56.860 --> 00:17:58.830
My name is Faust.

00:17:59.570 --> 00:18:02.300
I know you’re watching, Playmaker.

00:18:02.570 --> 00:18:03.790
Faust…

00:18:03.790 --> 00:18:05.770
Fight me.

00:18:05.770 --> 00:18:10.740
If you refuse, I'll defeat him 
and take his Cyberse card.

00:18:11.310 --> 00:18:14.970
Whatever!  I got that from Playmaker!

00:18:15.640 --> 00:18:17.720
Received it from Playmaker?

00:18:18.000 --> 00:18:19.950
Then duel me.

00:18:20.170 --> 00:18:22.210
Wait a second.

00:18:25.110 --> 00:18:30.670
Someone!  Someone save me!

00:18:30.670 --> 00:18:33.280
My name is Naoki Shima!

00:18:33.280 --> 00:18:36.740
I’ve been kidnapped and locked up!

00:18:36.740 --> 00:18:38.090
Locked up?

00:18:38.090 --> 00:18:42.350
Faust has kidnapped Shima in real life!

00:18:42.760 --> 00:18:46.040
Kusanagi, can you find Shima's location?

00:18:46.500 --> 00:18:49.920
I’ll try, but it'll take time.

00:18:49.920 --> 00:18:53.100
You go to LINK VRAINS and save him.

00:18:53.100 --> 00:18:54.500
Okay.

00:18:55.920 --> 00:18:57.520
My Duel Disk…

00:18:58.280 --> 00:19:00.960
I know I left it here.

00:19:02.220 --> 00:19:03.920
Hello, everyone!

00:19:05.240 --> 00:19:06.400
What’s this?

00:19:06.980 --> 00:19:09.380
Broadcasting from above Den City.

00:19:09.380 --> 00:19:11.140
Why are you…

00:19:11.140 --> 00:19:14.140
Wait a sec.  Umm…

00:19:17.140 --> 00:19:20.120
Ta daa!  Ai is on the scene!

00:19:20.120 --> 00:19:21.960
What’s going on?

00:19:21.960 --> 00:19:23.360
What are you doing?

00:19:24.440 --> 00:19:30.320
I had Idiotppi modify your Duel Disk.

00:19:30.720 --> 00:19:32.070
Roboppi?

00:19:32.650 --> 00:19:36.350
So that's why my Duel Disk felt heavy.

00:19:36.350 --> 00:19:38.100
I’ve gotten fat?

00:19:38.100 --> 00:19:39.330
I’m shocked!

00:19:39.330 --> 00:19:41.070
Come back right now!

00:19:41.360 --> 00:19:42.790
Are you sure?

00:19:42.790 --> 00:19:45.310
I’m trying to find Shima's location.

00:19:45.310 --> 00:19:46.870
Find?

00:19:46.870 --> 00:19:50.830
Den City is huge, so you 
won’t find him that easily-

00:19:50.830 --> 00:19:52.780
Cyberse Wizard's data!

00:19:52.780 --> 00:19:56.740
Correct!  I put a tracker on it.

00:19:57.160 --> 00:20:01.720
So you were prepared.  As if 
you knew this would happen.

00:20:02.070 --> 00:20:04.350
Are you accusing me?

00:20:04.350 --> 00:20:05.890
I’m shocked!

00:20:05.890 --> 00:20:07.720
So where’s Shima?

00:20:09.100 --> 00:20:13.360
I’ll send you his location signal.  
Switch the monitor to the map.

00:20:14.930 --> 00:20:16.390
Southeast.

00:20:20.860 --> 00:20:23.820
No more…  I’m sorry!

00:20:23.820 --> 00:20:26.950
I won’t get carried away again!  So please!

00:20:29.160 --> 00:20:31.370
Get on the board.

00:20:31.370 --> 00:20:33.390
Just let me go!

00:20:33.390 --> 00:20:38.350
Huh?  The one who carries on 
Playmaker’s will is a coward?

00:20:39.540 --> 00:20:42.400
Deep down inside, you’re scared.

00:20:42.400 --> 00:20:45.970
I appreciate your passion and 
enthusiasm.  But just those.

00:20:47.000 --> 00:20:48.960
Coward.

00:20:53.400 --> 00:20:54.910
I’ll do it!

00:20:55.550 --> 00:20:58.650
Emergency drone coming through.

00:20:58.650 --> 00:21:01.620
Commoners, move out of the way.

00:21:04.870 --> 00:21:07.070
That shape is stylish.

00:21:07.070 --> 00:21:09.580
I should also…

00:21:12.420 --> 00:21:14.440
Ouch!

00:21:15.810 --> 00:21:17.400
Pinpointed him yet?

00:21:17.400 --> 00:21:19.360
Found him!

00:21:19.360 --> 00:21:21.060
Straight ahead 7km!

00:21:21.440 --> 00:21:22.800
The warehouse district.

00:21:22.800 --> 00:21:25.260
Okay.  Ai, come back.

00:21:29.390 --> 00:21:34.720
TX625 requesting permission to land.  Over!

00:21:39.790 --> 00:21:41.390
Landing!

00:21:46.160 --> 00:21:48.130
Kusanagi, I leave the rest to you!

00:21:48.130 --> 00:21:48.940
Okay!

00:21:55.150 --> 00:21:58.510
Deck set!  Into the VRAINS!

00:22:00.250 --> 00:22:01.510
Shima…

00:22:08.620 --> 00:22:15.440
My life is like detestably bad graffiti

00:22:15.830 --> 00:22:22.580
But when you looked at 
me, I felt I wasn't alone

00:22:23.000 --> 00:22:29.780
I'm glad that I'm alive  I truly am

00:22:30.310 --> 00:22:37.160
What I couldn't say before, I can say now

00:22:38.010 --> 00:22:44.400
Within the sadness that I kept holding down

00:22:44.790 --> 00:22:48.530
There were fragments of power

00:22:48.790 --> 00:22:55.710
No one can take away my light to the future

00:22:55.970 --> 00:23:03.050
The chronicles of life only has a few lines

00:23:03.210 --> 00:23:10.260
People I meet, my regrets – they're 
all like ultramarine diamonds to me

00:23:10.510 --> 00:23:17.460
You've always confront loneliness by yourself

00:23:17.620 --> 00:23:24.340
I bet we can now laugh 
together, forever and ever

00:23:25.060 --> 00:23:32.040
Lighting Life with our invisible bond

00:23:36.110 --> 00:23:38.700
I wasn't without doubts.

00:23:38.700 --> 00:23:44.030
History has proven that scientific 
advancements require sacrifices.

00:23:44.030 --> 00:23:50.530
I've kept saying that to myself since the 
day the test succeeded, the day of my wrongdoing.

00:23:50.530 --> 00:23:55.710
But one who desires revenge 
won't listen to a researcher.

00:23:56.080 --> 00:23:58.850
Faust, I'm your opponent!

00:23:59.150 --> 00:24:03.150
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! VRAINS:
Final Commander of the Three Knights

00:24:03.150 --> 00:24:05.120
Into the VRAINS!
